  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 136 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nA warming trend continues in the Long Term period as mid level \nridging lies off to our west. Monday, the ridge is progged to be \ncentered near the Four Corners region. Afternoon highs will be \nsimilar to Sunday's, topping out in the upper 70s to low 80s. The \nridge builds eastward by midweek, increasing heights over our area. \nIn response, highs in the 80s become more commonplace through the \nremainder of the work week. Overnight lows are forecast to fall \nmainly into the 50s Monday night, then upper 50s to low 60s the \nrest of the period. Rain chances look low to none through the \nweek, given dry northwesterly flow aloft.",
